id: pm-7gpx34
title: "GH-1528: recover completeness and TOON mistakes on the attempted read command"
description: "Wrong-command completeness spellings and --toon currently point at other commands or lose intent. Provide a typed SDK recovery resolver consumed by CLI guidance: context --full becomes --depth full; list/search --depth full becomes --full; read --toon becomes --output-format toon. Preserve all operands, tracker selection and unrelated options; refuse ambiguous or conflicting rewrites."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,read-output,recovery
created_at: "2026-10-21T07:16:02.980Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T10:17:53.182Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#a064f14a96b4e8187e80e76b"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: The SDK emits shell-free same-command retries for GH1528 completeness and TOON cases; retries execute successfully in isolated trackers with whitespace operands and preserve authoritative bytes; conflicting or ambiguous options receive no unsafe retry; docs explain canonical controls and explicit format selection
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "Read-option refusals retain presentation intent even when command discovery did not resolve a command, and exact coverage remains complete."
