comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T07:16:02.980Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete 3038-item all-status corpus, request-specific search and live open/in-progress inventories found existing umbrella pm-f05lsg and grammar owner pm-n7rr but no leaf for GH1528. Existing issue comment links both owners. This bounded child implements the concrete recovery gap without claiming the entire grammar/recovery programme."
  "2026-10-21T07:19:59.430Z","harness:codex","Implementation plan: preserve command identity and argv tokens through an SDK resolver, prioritize verified semantic replacement over lexical guesses, and decline conflicting controls. New isolated integration regression executes emitted retries and compares all authoritative tracker bytes. The broad format-alias consolidation remains under pm-srns/pm-n7rr."
  "2026-10-21T07:44:40.806Z","harness:codex","Regression proof: the final integration test was copied unchanged into an isolated worktree at main 2a1e7dab0d34dc725d0b3b18e3cb9a49e82ec1c9 and failed because context --full did not emit suggested_retry_args. On the implementation, all six read correction cases execute successfully with whitespace search operands and explicit tracker/extension selection; authoritative tracker bytes remain identical. Unit controls decline malformed, conflicting, duplicate and cross-command rewrites."
  "2026-10-21T09:30:38.205Z","harness:codex","Final focused acceptance: all linked SDK/CLI regressions pass, including supported-option no-rewrite and malformed/conflicting/duplicate/path-mismatch controls. Emitted completeness and TOON retries preserve search operands, tracker selection, extension suppression and authoritative item/history bytes. This child delivers the concrete GH1528 recovery gap; uniform alias consolidation remains on the existing grammar/output owners."
  "2026-10-21T10:16:33.647Z","harness:codex","PR #1531 first head passed all 10,943 executed tests locally and all hosted coverage shards, but exact coverage correctly rejected one missing statement/branch in unresolved-command guidance. Added a boundary regression asserting no invented retry and top-level help when no command resolves. The unchanged graph census now passes at the existing 1,233 ceiling after linking real grammar owners and removing an incidental historical example; no quality threshold changed. CodeRabbit completed a full review with no actionable findings; optional providers report quota/trial limits."
  "2026-10-21T10:17:53.182Z","harness:codex","Revised linked acceptance passed 26 tests, including the new unresolved-command refusal boundary. The package-owned changelog flow uses pm-changelog 2026.10.21, now the latest published version; its semantic managed-extension version change is retained. Source changes do not alter dependency cooldowns or the single automatic daily publication policy."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T09:30:40.518Z","harness:codex","A semantic read-option correction must outrank lexical guesses, keep the attempted command and argv tokens, and decline conflicting presentation controls rather than discarding the requested intent."
